# Generators

Always use `yarn tempo g ...` instead of hand-creating files, so folders, tests, barrels and locale files match the structure lint.

| Command                                                        | Creates                                                                                      |
| -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `yarn tempo g feature <kebab-name>`                            | Feature tree, `src/locales/{en,ar}/<feature>.json`, `specs/<feature>/{spec,design,tasks}.md` |
| `yarn tempo g screen <Name> --feature <f> [--stack <Stack>]`   | `screens/<Name>Screen/` (screen, test, styles, index) and the route in `navigation/types.ts` |
| `yarn tempo g component <Name> [--feature <f>]`                | Component folder (shared components also get a story and a test)                             |
| `yarn tempo g hook <name>`, `g store <name>`, `g query <name>` | Hook, Zustand store, or query/mutation with keys, plus tests                                 |

Generated output passes `yarn verify` untouched. Overrides for the templates live in `.tempo/templates/<kind>/`.

After generating:

1. Fill in the code and the `en` **and** `ar` locale keys.
2. Register the route (or pass `--register`) and add the feature scope to `commitlint.config.mjs`.
3. Run `yarn verify:changed`.

## When the CLI is not installed

The CLI arrives with the template tooling. If `yarn tempo` does not exist yet, create the same files by hand and follow `architecture.md` and `naming.md` exactly: every file the generator would create (component/screen test, `styles.ts`, `index.ts`, locales in both languages) is required by lint anyway.

```
# ✅
yarn tempo g screen ItemDetails --feature items --stack Home

# ❌ hand-made screen folder with no test, no index.ts, no ar locale
```
